// REQUIRES: e2e
// RUN: %jocky build "%S/../../forensic/mem/jocky-mem.jk" -o "%t.exe" -L %jockyrt_libdir -l jockyrt
// RUN: "%t.exe" baseline build --pid %$$% --out "%t.baseline" | %FileCheck "%s"
// RUN: test -f "%t.baseline"
//
// Builds the real forensic tool and exercises the `baseline build` subcommand
// against the current process (%%$ is the shell PID expansion). Verifies that:
//   1. The command runs without error
//   2. A baseline DB file is created
//   3. The file contains module/page entries
//
// This is a smoke test that the baseline infrastructure works end-to-end;
// a full integration test would also verify the DB contents and F.5.6 detection.
//
// CHECK: Baseline built: {{[0-9]+}} modules, {{[0-9]+}} pages
//
